 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Valuative lifting for the two-open candidate",
 "statement": "Let $A$ be a valuation ring with fraction field $K$. Every commutative\ndiagram whose generic map\n$\\operatorname{Spec}(K)\\to W$ factors through $U_1\\cap U_2$ has a unique\nlift $\\operatorname{Spec}(A)\\to W$ over $S$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-thm-nagata-sketch-two-open/lemma-nagata-two-open-valuative-lifting.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-two-open-valuative-lifting, order 303"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By\n[lemma-nagata-proper-separated-valuation-extension], properness and\nseparatedness of $X_i\\to S$ extend the generic map to maps\n$g_i\\colon\\operatorname{Spec}(A)\\to X_i$. By\n[lemma-nagata-one-valuation-avoids-boundary], one extension factors\nthrough $X_i\\setminus\\overline Z_{i,j}$ and hence through $W_i$. The\ngeneric map already lifts to the preserved open $U\\subseteq W'_i$.\nThe admissible blow-up $W'_i\\to W_i$ is proper, hence separated, so\n[lemma-nagata-proper-separated-valuation-extension] supplies a lift\nto $W'_i$; its open map to $W$ gives the desired lift. Any two branch\nchoices have the same generic restriction. Since $W\\to S$ is separated by\n[lemma-nagata-two-open-final-modification],\n[lemma-nagata-separated-valuation-lift-unique] makes the two maps\nequal.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-proper-separated-valuation-extension",
    "lemma-nagata-one-valuation-avoids-boundary",
    "lemma-nagata-two-open-final-modification",
    "lemma-nagata-separated-valuation-lift-unique"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
